<title>FRANCE: French 1997 grain/oilseed sowing estimates.</title>
<headline>French 1997 grain/oilseed sowing estimates.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a breakdown of winter and spring grain sowing estimates in hectares published by the French farm ministry on Monday.</p>
<p>The figures do not include forecasts for maize and sorghum.</p>
<p>The ministry projected 1997 soft wheat sowings would exceed 4.9 million hectares, approaching a 1984 record.</p>
<p>The rise is spread across most regions and especially the Champagne-Ardenne region in eastern France, and Pays de Loire and Poitou-Charentes in the west.</p>
<p>Winter barley sowing increases were strongest in central France and in the Poitou-Charentes region.</p>
<p>After falling for two consecutive years, spring barley sowings are on the rise across France.</p>
